# 01 — Data Preprocessing Pipeline

This notebook implements the preprocessing workflow for imbalance-aware financial distress prediction under severe minority-class sparsity conditions.

The preprocessing pipeline incorporates:

- dataset loading,
- missing-value handling,
- deterministic train-test partitioning,
- feature scaling,
- correlation-aware feature inspection,
- class imbalance analysis,
- and reproducibility-oriented preprocessing controls.

The workflow is aligned with CRISP-DM-oriented machine learning engineering practices and supports downstream imbalance-aware optimisation procedures.

import pandas as pd
import numpy as np

from sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split
from sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler

import matplotlib.pyplot as plt
import seaborn as sns

RANDOM_STATE = 42

np.random.seed(RANDOM_STATE)

df = pd.read_csv("../data/bankruptcy_data.csv")

df.head()

print("Dataset Shape:")
print(df.shape)

print("\nMissing Values:")
print(df.isnull().sum().sort_values(ascending=False).head())

class_counts = df["Bankrupt?"].value_counts()

print(class_counts)

plt.figure(figsize=(6,4))

sns.countplot(
    x="Bankrupt?",
    data=df
)

plt.title("Class Distribution Before SMOTE")

plt.xlabel("Bankruptcy Class")
plt.ylabel("Observation Count")

plt.show()

X = df.drop("Bankrupt?", axis=1)

y = df["Bankrupt?"]

X_train, X_test, y_train, y_test = train_test_split(
    X,
    y,
    test_size=0.2,
    stratify=y,
    random_state=RANDOM_STATE
)

print(X_train.shape)
print(X_test.shape)

scaler = StandardScaler()

X_train_scaled = scaler.fit_transform(X_train)

X_test_scaled = scaler.transform(X_test)

corr_matrix = X.corr().abs()

upper_triangle = corr_matrix.where(
    np.triu(np.ones(corr_matrix.shape), k=1).astype(bool)
)

high_corr_features = [
    column
    for column in upper_triangle.columns
    if any(upper_triangle[column] > 0.95)
]

print(high_corr_features)

# Preprocessing Summary

The preprocessing workflow incorporated:

- deterministic train-test partitioning,
- class-aware stratified sampling,
- feature scaling,
- correlation-aware inspection,
- and reproducibility-oriented preprocessing controls.

The severe minority-class imbalance observed within the dataset further reinforces the need for imbalance-aware optimisation procedures explored in subsequent notebooks.
